  <footer class="notes">
    <h2>Method &amp; caveats</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every date above was pulled live from the university's own admissions or institute page (via Firecrawl), not from aggregator sites or social posts, except where marked "status unclear."</li>
      <li>The three countries run on different clocks. Turkish and Pakistani universities intake mainly in Fall and take applications roughly February–August, so several are still open in July. Indian institutions front-load their international-student cycle to November–April for a July intake — every Indian program below is closed for now and reopens around January–April 2027.</li>
      <li>Tuition/program details shift often. Treat every deadline here as a starting point for verification, not a final answer — re-check the linked page before relying on a date to plan around.</li>
      <li>"Turkish" tags mean Turkish is the primary language of instruction — several (Kocaeli, YTÜ) still require some English coursework or proficiency at admission. Only Hacettepe's Turkish tag comes from an explicit department statement; YTÜ, Sinop, and Kocaeli are inferred from each university's general graduate-language pattern and are worth a direct confirmation if language is a dealbreaker.</li>
      <li>Pakistan and India programs are shown here as MS/M.Tech in Computer Engineering or the closest equivalent (Computer Science, Computer Science &amp; Engineering) — naming varies by country more than in Turkey.</li>
    </ul>
  </footer>

